ready: 1
kind: sequence
id: sync.seq.sync
display_id: SEQ-SYNC
module: sync
title: Sync a stack with the cloud
summary: Pushes this stack's confirmed-pending changes first, then pulls the cloud's changes page by page and applies them with the conflict rule.
trigger:
  trigger_kind: call
  text: The owner runs sync, push, or pull, an agent calls the sync tool, or the scheduler syncs a linked stack
operation: sync.op.sync
participants:
  - sys.daemon
  - sys.cloud
  - sys.home
items: []
parts: [sync.seq.sync.a, sync.seq.sync.b]
rationale: >-
  Push runs before pull so a local edit is in the cloud before the cloud's
  view is applied, which keeps the conflict rule's inputs honest. Pull uses the
  cloud's own cursor and pages, because a local clock can skip changes written
  during a pull and a fixed page size silently truncates large stacks.
